FINANCE OFFICE
Assistant Purchasing Manager (26270265)
The appointee will assist in managing the procurement function and oversee the daily administration of the University’s Auxiliary Services (including carpool, mail and courier services).
Responsibilities:
Assist the Senior Purchasing Manager / Purchasing Manager in the management of the procurement function;
Supervise the Purchasing Officers / Assistant Purchasing Officers for the daily routine procurement tasks;
Oversee the daily operation of the Auxiliary Services and follow up on operational issues;
Provide administrative support for insurance-related matters, including maintaining records, coordinating documentation and renewals, assisting with claims, and liaising with insurers, brokers and internal units as required;
Manage and monitor tender and quotation exercises, ensuring compliance with the University’s procurement policies and procedures and the timely completion of procurement activities;
Conduct procurement analyses, compile management reports and board papers;
Liaise with internal departments and suppliers for implementing cost-effective purchasing initiatives or special projects; and
Any other procurement and administration duties assigned by the Senior Purchasing Manager / Purchasing Manager.
Requirements:
A recognised bachelor’s degree or above with at least 5 years relevant working experience of which 3 years in supervisory role is essential;
Proven experience in a sizeable procurement organisation is a must, and prior engagement in the educational institutions is preferred;
Experience overseeing operational services, such as carpool, mail and courier services, and/or providing insurance administrative support would be an advantage;
Professional qualification in procurement or supply chain management is a definite advantage;
Possess a can-do attitude, pleasant personality, impeccable integrity, excellent communication and problem-solving skills;
Be well-organised, proactive and service-oriented; and
Able to work both independently and as a good team player.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract of two years. Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to mutual agreement and availability of funding.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 8 weeks after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University's Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

ACADEMIC REGISTRY
Senior Executive Officer (26270291)
The Academic Registry is now looking for motivated and experienced applicants to join the Admissions Office.
Responsibilities:
Support the end-to-end operation of undergraduate admissions, including reviewing and vetting applications, communicating with applicants and academic units, issuing offers, verifying documentation, and facilitating enrolment procedures;
Serve as a primary liaison for applicants and Faculties/Schools, facilitate effective communication and coordination throughout the admissions process;
Prepare and compile statistical analysis and reports;
Coordinate and support local or non-local outreach activities and University-wide events;
Coordinate digital marketing campaign; manage agencies and designers in creating engaging promotional materials and content tailored for different markets;
Occasional participation in duty trips are expected; and
Perform other duties as assigned.
Requirements:
A recognised degree plus preferably three to five years of post-qualification work experience;
Experience in the tertiary education sector, particularly in Non-JUPAS admissions, is highly advantageous;
Strong attention to detail and a high level of IT proficiency, especially in Power BI and implementing automation solutions, will be an asset;
Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); and
Self-motivated, with a positive work attitude, the ability to work independently, and to perform well under pressure.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test.
The initial appointment will be offered on a fixed-term contract of two year(s). Re-appointment thereafter will be subject to mutual agreement.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 8 weeks after the closing date may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Closing date: 11 November 2026

In a city renowned for its international outlook and connectivity, The Hong Kong Academy for Performing Arts (HKAPA) plays a unique and influential role in nurturing future generations of performing artists, including performers, practitioners, designers, and technicians. Ranked 10th in the 2026 QS World University Rankings for Performing Arts and 1st in Asia, the Academy and its Schools of Chinese Opera, Dance, Drama, Film & Television, Music, and Theatre & Entertainment Arts form a vibrant centre of practice, production, teaching, and practice-as-research. Its outstanding reputation is reinforced by the quality of its graduates and its partnerships with centres of excellence locally, regionally, and internationally. Through international residencies, visiting artists, and a distinguished alumni network—including some of the most respected professionals in their disciplines—the Academy is committed to training future world-class performers and practitioners.
As HKAPA is entering an exciting new phase of development, including plans for a new campus in the Northern Metropolis, we are looking for an organised and detail-minded administrator to provide a spectrum of executive service to support the various campus development initiatives and operations.
The postholder will support the planning and implementation of campus development and capital works projects, assist in liaison with internal and external stakeholders, and provide secretarial support to project teams, committees and working groups, management decision-making, and contribute to the enhancement of administrative processes and systems.
Applicants should have:
(a) A recognised bachelor's degree or equivalent qualification;
(b) Normally, at least five years’ relevant work experience preferably in higher education institutions, public organisations, government bodies or comparable environments;
(c) Strong analytical, organisational, communication and stakeholder management skills, with sound judgement and the ability to manage multiple priorities;
(d) Experience in drafting, reviewing and coordinating official documents, reports and committee papers;
(e) Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic environment;
(f) Excellent command of spoken and written English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua);
(g) Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and other relevant digital platforms; and
(h) Experience in governance and committee administration, institutional approval processes, campus development or capital works projects will be an advantage.
TERMS OF APPOINTMENT
The initial appointment will be made on a two-year contract. Renewal thereafter will be subject to satisfactory performance, operational needs, and the availability of funding. A gratuity payment may be granted upon satisfactory completion of the full contract. Fringe benefits include leave, medical, and dental benefits. The starting salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application To apply, please submit a completed Application Form ( click_here ), together with a cover letter, curriculum vitae and copies of academic qualifications, to the Human Resources Office, The Hong Kong Academy for Performing Arts, No.1 Gloucester Road, Wanchai, Hong Kong, or email (hro@hkapa.edu) on or before 15 November 2026. The application documents should be combined into one file in PDF format. Please quote reference code ' EO(SP) ' in the Application Form. Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted.
HKAPA is an equal opportunity employer.
Personal data collected will be used for recruitment-related purposes only.

