OFFICE OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY
Senior Digital Experience Specialist (26270060)
The Senior Digital Experience Specialist will collaborate with internal IT staff and business units to support the migration of legacy websites to Adobe Experience Cloud or alternative CMS solutions. With a business analyst mindset, this specialist will leverage expertise in contemporary digital solutions, proactively identifying and resolving challenges faced during the migration process.
Responsibilities:
Partner with internal IT team members and other stakeholders to coordinate and support the migration of legacy websites to Adobe Experience Cloud or alternative CMS platforms;
Demonstrate strong knowledge of various CMS solutions in the market (such as Adobe Experience Cloud, Wix Enterprise, WordPress, Drupal, Sitecore, etc.) and assist in evaluating their suitability for organisational needs;
Understand and address technical migration challenges, including security considerations, DNS settings, VPN requirements, and other infrastructure concerns;
Act as a key contact for troubleshooting migration issues, ensuring clear communication among IT staff and business users, and proactively resolving blockers in collaboration with the delivery team;
Support the Digital Enablement and Solution Manager (DESM) in the exploration of digital experience products, including but not limited to enhancements and integrations such as Customer Journey Analytics (CJA) and Adobe Journey Optimiser (AJO);
Assist the DESM in the preparation of presentations, proposals, and solution comparisons to inform decision making for management and internal stakeholders;
Adopt a presales mindset for internal users by helping align stakeholders on a value-based prioritisation of requested solutions;
Collect and clarify business requirements from internal users, translate them into actionable user stories/acceptance criteria, and drive alignment with IT and delivery teams to meet demand;
Occasionally lead solution enablement initiatives end-to-end—from intake and planning through execution, testing, go-live, and closure—ensuring outcomes meet internal user requirements; and
Take up other IT projects and assignments as assigned.
Requirements:
A bachelor’s degree in computer science, information systems, or related disciplines;
At least 5-6 years of post-graduate experience in digital experience, business analysis, or similar roles;
Hands-on experience with website migrations and multiple CMS platforms, including Adobe Experience Cloud and alternatives;
Ability to analyse and compare digital solutions, considering organisational requirements, technical complexity, and integration potential;
Strong problem-solving skills, with demonstrated ability to address security, DNS, VPN, and related technical challenges;
Excellent communication and presentation skills, including the ability to support and co-create materials for management review;
Experience supporting internal solution enablement, requirements gathering, and delivery coordination with cross-functional team; and
Awareness of ESG principles and digital accessibility standards is an asset.
Shortlisted candidates will be invited to sit for a written test.
The initial appointment will be made on a fixed-term contract of two years. Re-appointment thereafter is subject to performance review, mutual agreement and availability of funding.
Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Application Procedure:
Applicants are invited to submit their applications at the HKBU e-Recruitment System. Those who are not invited for interview 8 weeks after submission of application may consider their applications unsuccessful. Details of the University’s Personal Information Collection Statement can be found at https://hro.hkbu.edu.hk/en/worklife-at-hkbu/employee-favourable-environment.html#privacy-policy.
The University reserves the right not to make an appointment for the post advertised, and the appointment will be made according to the terms and conditions applicable at the time of offer.
Review of applications is ongoing until the position is filled.

Tung Wah College
Tung Wah College (TWC) is a self-financing tertiary institution incorporated in 2010 by the Tung Wah Group of Hospitals (TWGHs). Drawing on TWGHs’ recognised strengths and expertise in medical and health services, education, and social services, TWC aspires to become a leading University of Applied Sciences in the Asia-Pacific region. By integrating education, research and industry partnerships, TWC nurtures compassionate, innovative leaders who are ready for a changing world. TWC is an approved post-secondary college registered under the Post Secondary Colleges Ordinance (Cap 320). All TWC programmes are accredited by the Hong Kong Council for Accreditation of Academic and Vocational Qualifications (HKCAAVQ).
TWC currently offers postgraduate, degree, sub-degree, and certificate programmes through four Schools: the School of Nursing, the School of Medical and Health Sciences, the School of Management, and the School of Arts and Humanities. The College has a student population of over 6,100. Its programmes cover nursing, gerontology, health information and services management, biomedical science, forensic biomedical science, medical laboratory science, occupational therapy, physiotherapy, radiation therapy, medical imaging, management in social and business sustainability, applied psychology, early childhood education, and other disciplines.
As TWC continues to develop, we plan to introduce new programmes, enhance our teaching and learning facilities and quality, and strengthen our research capabilities in the coming years. We warmly invite suitably qualified candidates to join us on this journey and contribute to the College’s next chapter of development through the following position:
Duties and Responsibilities
The appointee will be required but not limited to:
Assist in implementation of new Human Resources system such as Performance and Goal Management, provide support in the enhancement works, in particular, testing work, perform data checking, ensure data accuracy and any other related tasks;
Assist in providing medical and leave benefits administration to ensure consistency, compliance, and accuracy. Verify medical claims for payroll purposes;
Provide account servicing support to designated units in the area of human resources management, including recruitment and selection, performance management, compensation and benefits administration, employee relations and staff development;
Assist in preparing management reports, HR related statistics reports and analysis to internal departments and external authorities;
Provide answers to enquiries from staff on Human Resources system as well as benefits;and
Other duties as assigned by supervisors.
Qualifications and Experience Required
Applicants should possess / be:
A Bachelor’s degree in human resources management or related disciplines;
3 years of relevant working experience in human resources management, preferably gained in the tertiary institutions or public bodies;
Experience with SAP or similar ERP systems is preferred;
Knowledge of Employment Ordinance and other HR related legislations;
High level of proficiency in Excel and other IT applications;
Good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese;
A proactive team player who is helpful, supportive, and thrives in a collaborative office culture;
Logical thinking, detail-minded and have good organization and interpersonal skills; and
Demonstrated ability to work effectively across different departments and provide good service to staff members.
Application
Salary will be competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience.
To apply, please submit your application via system. The College reserves the right to fill or not to fill the post. Applicants who are not contacted by the College 6 months after the application deadline may consider their applications unsuccessful. For enquiries, please phone or send WhatsApp to 9172-8618.
Application Deadline: Until the position is filled
All information and personal data collected will be used solely for recruitment related purposes. For more information about the College, please visit our website: http://www.twc.edu.hk .
WE ARE AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER

The Hong Kong Institute for the Humanities and Social Sciences (IHSS) invites applications for the position of Part-time Teaching Assistant (Ref. 537652) for the Common Core course CCGL9069: Multinationals and the Global Economy , for Semester 2 of the 2026-27 academic year. The appointment period is between January and May 2027. The course outline can be found here: https://commoncore.hku.hk/ccgl9069/
Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree or above in History, Economics, Business, Global Studies, International Political Economy, Social Sciences, or a related discipline. Preference will be given to current or recent postgraduate students or candidates with prior experience in teaching, tutoring, student assessment or research experience in areas related to globalization, multinational corporations, international business, economic history, global capitalism, or related fields.
Applicants should also have excellent communication and interpersonal skills, a strong command of written and spoken English, and the ability to facilitate discussion-based learning among undergraduate students. Experience in grading coursework and providing academic feedback will be an advantage.
The appointee will assist the course instructor in the delivery of CCGL9069: Multinationals and the Global Economy . Duties will include:
Conducting and facilitating tutorial classes;
Leading discussions on course themes and readings;
Marking and providing feedback on student assessments, including tutorial presentations, reflective journals, group projects, and class participation;
Assisting in the preparation of tutorial materials and learning activities;
Holding consultation sessions and providing academic support to students as required;
Assisting with course administration and other teaching-related duties assigned by the course instructor.
Remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience.
Applicants should submit a cover letter and an up-to-date curriculum vitae alongside their application via the system. Review of applications will commence immediately and continue until November 14, 2026 , or until the post is filled. Shortlisted candidates may be invited to attend an interview.
For enquiries about the position, please contact Professor Ghassan Moazzin, at gmoazzin@hku.hk.

LIBRARY
Library Assistant (26270297)
The University Library is seeking a Library Assistant for its Special Collections and Archives (SCA) team at the Au Shue Hung Memorial Library (Main Library). This is an excellent opportunity for individuals passionate about user and reference services, digitisation, and the management of special and archival collections.
The SCA team manages four core collections: the Archives on the History of Christianity in China, Contemporary China Research Collection, the University Archives, and Special Collections. Our Special Collections include rare books, personal papers and organisational records, art collections, etc.
Responsibilities:
