Plan WM service facilities and development;
Ensure that the daily clinical operation of the WM division complies with the Applicable Laws and licensing requirements;
Handle patient complaints and related medical incidents;
Manage WM and support Chinese medicine research and education;
Manage staff of WM division;
Support service planning and development of the Hospital; and
Assist in the development and implementation of organisation policies and plans.
Requirements:
A postgraduate degree;
Registered medical practitioner under the Medical Registration Ordinance (Cap. 161), and must have been registered for not less than fifteen years in Hong Kong;
Must have substantial hands-on hospital management experience in Hong Kong;
A highly motivated dynamic leader with a strong commitment to achieving strategic results;
Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to promote collaboration with local and international parties; and
Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese.
